11. The Required Prediction Ledger

If Amodei’s claims are to support legislation, military strategy, industrial policy and enormous infrastructure commitments, they should be registered as measurable forecasts rather than preserved as literary possibilities.

Public claim	Required operational definition
Powerful AI as early as 2026 or likely around 2027	A fixed battery covering cross-domain Nobel-level performance, autonomous task completion, reliability, grounding and real-world execution
“Country of geniuses”	Number of independent instances, coordination capacity, memory, error rate, human supervision and actual completed work
Fifty per cent of entry-level white-collar jobs disrupted within one to five years	Countries, occupations, baseline employment level and whether “disrupted” means task change, vacancy reduction or net job elimination
Reliable interpretability within five to ten years	Detection probability, false-positive rate and predefined classes of hidden behaviour
Fifty to one hundred years of biological progress in five to ten years	A preregistered index of therapies, mortality reductions, approvals, mechanisms and validated discoveries
Most cancer eliminated	Cancer types, incidence, mortality, geography and deadline
Human lifespan doubled	Cohort, intervention, survival measure and verification date
AI creates extreme economic growth	Real GDP, productivity, distribution and comparison baseline

Without definitions like these, almost every forecast survives.

“Could arrive as early as 2026” survives if it does not.

“Disrupted” survives whether jobs disappear or merely acquire a chatbot.

“Fifty years of progress” survives because no standard unit of scientific progress exists.

“Powerful AI” survives by moving the capability threshold.

A prophecy that cannot lose is not a forecast.

It is brand architecture.

